      "text": "To find all the integer values of \\( a \\) such that the polynomial \n\\[ x^3 + 3x^2 + ax + 7 = 0 \\]\nhas at least one integer root, we use the Factor Theorem. If \\( c \\) is an integer root of the polynomial, then \\( (x - c) \\) is a factor of the polynomial, and thus \\( x^3 + 3x^2 + ax + 7 \\) can be written as:\n\\[ (x - c)(x^2 + (b + c)x + ec) \\]\nwhere \\( b = 3 \\) and \\( e = 7 \\). So, the polynomial becomes:\n\\[ (x - c)(x^2 + (3 + c)x + 7) \\]\n\nExpanding this product, we get:\n\\[ x^3 + (3 + c)x^2 + (7 - 5c)x - 7c \\]\n\nWe want this to be equal to the original polynomial \\( x^3 + 3x^2 + ax + 7 \\). Therefore, we compare coefficients:\n\\[ x^3 + 3x^2 + ax + 7 = x^3 + (3 + c)x^2 + (7 - 5c)x - 7c \\]\n\nBy comparing the coefficients of like terms, we get:\n1. The coefficient of \\( x^2 \\):\n\\[ 3 = 3 + c \\]\nSolving for \\( c \\):\n\\[ 3c = 0 \\]\n\\[ c = 0 \\]\n\n2. The coefficient of \\( x \\):\n\\[ a = 7 - 5c \\]\nSubstituting \\( c = 0 \\):\n\\[ a = 7 - 5(0) \\]\n\\[ a = 7 \\]\n\n3. Lastly, the constant term:\n\\[ 7 = -7c \\]\nAgain, solving for \\( c \\):\n\\[ 7 = -7c \\]\n\\[ c = -1 \\]\n\nBy comparing different values of \\( c \\):\n- For \\( c = 0 \\), we found \\( a = 7 \\)\n- For \\( c = -1 \\), we find \\( a = 7 - (7 \\cdot -1) = 7 + 7 = 14 \\)\n\nWe now verify the integer roots for these values of \\( c \\):\n\nFor \\( c = 0 \\):\nThe polynomial becomes \\( x^3 + 3x^2 + 7 \\). We test integer roots:\n- \\( a = 0 \\):\n  \\[ x^3 + 3x^2 + 0 = x^3 + 3x^2 \\]\n  Testing integer roots:\n  \\[ x - 0 = 0 \\implies x = 0 \\]\n  Thus, \\( x = 0 \\) is a root.\n\nFor \\( c = -1 \\):\nThe polynomial becomes \\( x^3 + 3x^2 - 14 \\). We test integer roots:\n- \\( a = -14 \\):\n  \\[ x^3 + 3x^2 - 14 = x^3 + 3x^2 - 14 \\]\n  Testing integer roots:\n  \\[ x - (-1) = x + 1 \\]\n  \\( x = -1 \\) is a root.\n\nSo, by verifying, both solutions \\( a = 7 \\) and \\( a = 14 \\) are correct as they satisfy the original polynomial equation when we test integer roots.\n\nHence, the integer values of \\( a \\) are:\n\\[ \\boxed{7, 14} \\]",
